{
  "title": "Do not ignore current-head review feedback received during submit \
hooks",
  "description": "The shared agent-submit command invokes issue_watch_pr.run \
only after after_publish hooks finish, and that watcher snapshots all existing \
feedback as baseline_feedback. A review of the newly pushed commit arriving \
during a long make signoff hook is therefore silently treated as old feedback. \
Transferred from Block Descent issue p2-agent-submit-review-during-hooks. \
Observed on https://github.com/GregorStocks/block-descent/pull/189: review \
5123867679 for head 460cb5f arrived at 2026-09-06T02:47:18Z while the newly \
required balance report was running; after signoff the watcher repeatedly \
printed waiting for codex and did not surface the unresolved current-head \
comment. Fix this in the shared agent-issues tooling by capturing the feedback \
baseline before publishing/hooks or by distinguishing current-head feedback \
from previously handled reviews. Add a regression test with feedback arriving \
during an after-publish hook. Do not bypass the repository signoff hook to \
avoid the race.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "tooling",
    "agent-issues",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-09-06T02:56:50Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-09-06T18:26:23Z",
}
